  "scope": [
    "The exact CurrentJets zero-order clause chooses one loss and one positive B before all pieces, atoms and unit points.",
    "The same original T.H and T.E0 at exactly T.sample(K.cell m) obey the true positive-height-power absorption estimate. No equality between sample cells is assumed.",
    "For any positive delta the actual radius min(epsilon,delta/(2*B*CH)) and base max(base,loss) make every true atom difference strictly smaller than delta, uniformly.",
    "The original full CurrentJets tower is restricted using the existing proved neighborhood theorem; no synthetic directional derivatives or separate atom family is chosen.",
    "The result can be applied at delta=1/4 for the cross-half range argument, but moving/reference domain membership and sample comparisons still require their actual geometric proofs."
